From 2664b82502ace674a7f085c16bc86361b870ab0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathaniel Phelps <natezmcpherson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 18:04:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kcm/mouse: Add custom acceleration curve editor

GUI for libinput's custom pointer acceleration profile, building on kwin!6937.

Features:
    Bezier curve editor with 4 draggable control points
    Sensitivity Y axis (1.0 = physical match)
    Extension arrow for linear continuation beyond curve end
    Presets: Dynamic, Linear, Gentle, Aggressive with auto Custom detection
    Zoom controls for both axes

Review fixes:
    1. Remove evdev speed monitor (security, inputspeedmonitor.cpp)
        Reading /dev/input directly requires input group membership.
        Keep visualization code, wire to KWin D-Bus speed interface when available.
    4. Remove precision truncation in serializeCurve()
        Output is not user-facing, use full float precision.
    7. curvePresets changed from object to array, loop uses .length (Jakob)

Depends on: kwin!6937
CCBUG: 464868
